📋 Step-by-Step Instructions:
1. Backend Server (Already Running)
# The backend is running on http://localhost:3001
# Health check: http://localhost:3001/api/health
# API docs: http://localhost:3001/api-docs
2. Start Frontend (React App)
cd client
npm start
# This will start the React app on http://localhost:3000
3. Optional: Start n8n (for workflow execution)
# If you have n8n installed globally:
n8n start

# Or using Docker:
docker run -it --rm --name n8n -p 5678:5678 n8nio/n8n
🌐 Application URLs:
Frontend: http://localhost:3000
Backend API: http://localhost:3001/api
API Documentation: http://localhost:3001/api-docs
Health Check: http://localhost:3001/api/health
n8n (optional): http://localhost:5678
🧪 Testing the Application:
Manual Testing:
Open http://localhost:3000
Login with demo@example.com / demo123
Explore the dashboard with pre-populated data
View sample workflows in the Workflows section
Check execution history in the Executions section
Test dark/light mode toggle
Test responsive design on different screen sizes
Automated Testing:
# Unit tests
npm test

# E2E tests (requires both frontend and backend running)
npm run test:e2e

# Open Cypress test runner
npm run test:e2e:open
🔧 Development Commands:
# Backend development
npm run dev                    # Start backend with hot reload
npm run build                  # Build backend for production
npm run test                   # Run backend tests

# Frontend development
cd client
npm start                      # Start frontend with hot reload
npm run build                  # Build frontend for production
npm run test                   # Run frontend tests
npm run test:e2e              # Run E2E tests

# Database operations
npm run db:generate           # Generate Prisma client
npm run db:push              # Push schema to database
npm run db:migrate           # Run migrations
npm run db:seed:test         # Seed test data
🎉 Features to Test:
Authentication: Login, logout, token refresh
Dashboard: Real-time metrics, charts, recent activity
Workflows: Create, edit, delete, execute workflows
Executions: Monitor real-time execution status and logs
UI/UX: Dark/light mode, responsive design, toast notifications
Performance: Fast loading, optimized queries, caching
🐛 Troubleshooting:
If you encounter issues:

Database connection errors: Ensure PostgreSQL is running on port 5432
Redis connection errors: Ensure Redis is running on port 6379 (optional)
Port conflicts: Check if ports 3000, 3001 are available
Module not found: Run npm install in both root and client directories
Prisma errors: Run npx prisma generate and npx prisma db push
The application is now fully functional with all the polish and optimization features implemented! 🎊